From c5adb95438c51ab6c160b47f656002c1b6a0d99c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:50:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] Closures need a complete list; crawl state and
 per-posting accounting for every board

server/history.js: updateLedger closes a posting only when absent from a complete list
(x: absent), on a probe's 404/410/redirect (x: gone), or after UNSEEN_OPEN_DAYS missing from
partial lists (x: unseen); listed-but-unpublished ids stay open. closureOptions builds the
options from a snapshot. scripts/snapshot.js: fetchBoard passes the previous crawl state
(MELON_CRAWL_STATE_DIR, <slug>.json.gz) to the adapter, normalizes the whole board, writes the
snapshot's crawl field (mode, list completeness, new/changed/unchanged/absent, gone) and the
next state. beta-snapshots.mjs merge reads the same crawl's listed ids. Stable adapters report
their response validators.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
